  #line-at(90.024pt, 412.61pt, "Abstract")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 428.21pt, "Mo/Si multilayer mirrors are central to extreme ultraviolet lithography, where ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 443.83pt, "nanoscale optical interference and heat accumulation together constrain reflectivity and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 459.43pt, "operational stability. Here we develop an analytical electromagnetic–thermal coupling ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 475.03pt, "model that directly links transfer-matrix-based interference-controlled energy ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 490.63pt, "deposition with transient heat conduction in EUV-irradiated multilayers. The model ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 506.23pt, "reveals a fundamental trade-off whereby increasing the multilayer period number ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 521.83pt, "enhances reflectivity but simultaneously elevates temperature by impeding heat ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 537.43pt, "dissipation. Interference-driven volumetric absorption further gives rise to pronounced ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 553.03pt, "axial temperature gradients and a post-pulse downward migration of the heat-flux ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 568.63pt, "maximum, a delayed-heating effect inaccessible to conventional surface-flux-based ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 584.23pt, "models. Systematic analysis establishes scaling laws connecting interfacial thermal ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 599.83pt, "resistance, beam size, and incident energy density to thermal confinement and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 615.43pt, "temperature rise. By incorporating interfacial compaction kinetics, the model enables a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 631.06pt, "quantitative assessment of mirror lifetime. This work offers a theoretical tool for ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 646.66pt, "thermal–optical co-design of multilayer nanostructures including EUV mirrors under ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 662.26pt, "pulsed irradiation across a wide spectral range. ")
]

