  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(111.02pt, 154.34pt, "In this work, we build the analytical model of interference-driven electromagnetic–")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 185.54pt, "thermal coupling based on a typical multilayer EUV mirror, schematically depicted in ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 216.74pt, "Fig. 1(a). The structure consists of a periodic Mo/amorphous-Si (a-Si) multilayer stack ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 247.94pt, "deposited on a crystalline-Si (c-Si) substrate, with a thin Ru capping layer on top. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 279.17pt, "Notably, the proposed coupling framework is readily extendable to other multilayer-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 310.37pt, "based optical systems. Conventional MHTM often treats the incident laser irradiation ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 341.57pt, "as a constant surface heat flux, as suggested in the inset of Fig. 1(a). However, in such ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 372.77pt, "periodic optical structures, the incident electromagnetic wave undergoes significant ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 403.97pt, "interference, which governs the spatial distribution of electromagnetic absorption and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 435.17pt, "the resulting non-uniform thermal response. Therefore, an accurate model must ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 466.39pt, "explicitly account for the wave propagation and interference within the multilayer stack. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 497.59pt, "To this end, the transfer matrix method is employed to describe the electromagnetic ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 528.79pt, "distributions, in which the electromagnetic field is decomposed into downward- and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 559.99pt, "upward-propagating waves, as follows: ")
